**Section 354 — Outraging modesty**: Assault or use of criminal force with intent to outrage modesty — up to 10 years OR fine OR whipping OR any two.

**Section 375 — Rape**: A man is said to commit rape who has sexual intercourse with a woman in any of the following circumstances:
(a) against her will;
(b) without her consent;
(c) with consent obtained by fear of death/hurt;
(d) with consent obtained by impersonating husband;
(e) with consent when she is under influence of intoxicant/unsound mind;
(f) with or without consent when under 16 years.

**Section 376 — Punishment for rape**: 5–30 years AND whipping. Aggravated: minimum 8 years.

**Section 377A — Carnal intercourse against order of nature**: Up to 20 years AND whipping.
**Section 377B**: Voluntarily committing — minimum 5 years, up to 20 AND whipping.
**Section 377C**: Without consent — 5–20 years AND whipping.
**Section 377CA**: Sexual connection by object — same penalty.
**Section 377D**: Outrages of decency — up to 2 years.
**Section 377E**: Inciting child to act of gross indecency — up to 5 years OR fine.

**Sexual Offences Against Children Act 2017**: Additional protections for minors.
